.TH MU2EDAQ-COMMANDLINE-TOOLS-STOP 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2edaq-commandline-tools.sh \- stop a running tool and clean up
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./stop-mu2edaq-commandline-tools.sh
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the pidfile written by
.BR start-mu2edaq-commandline-tools.sh (1),
sends SIGTERM, waits for a clean exit, and sends SIGKILL if the process is
still alive when the timeout expires. Then removes the pidfile, any
.I __pycache__
directories in the checkout, and the log directory.
.PP
It is not an error to run this when nothing is running; a stale pidfile is
reported and removed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " \fISECS\fR"
Seconds to wait after SIGTERM before sending SIGKILL. Default:
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-logs
Leave the log directory in place.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_PIDFILE
Pidfile location. Default:
.I .mu2edaq-tools.pid
in the checkout.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_DIR
Log directory to remove. Default:
.I logs
in the checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including when there was nothing to stop.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-start (1),
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
